abstract: >-
  Traditional programming languages (C, Go, Rust, Python) are designed around human biological constraints:
  low-bandwidth keyboard input and visual ASCII source reading, which impose a massive serialization,
  parsing, type-inference, and LLVM optimization tax on autonomous AI Agents. Rul (.rl) eliminates textual
  source code as the primary representation, replacing it with a memory-mapped flat binary topological
  SSA-DAG where every instruction is a fixed 128-bit (16-byte) NodeFrame encoding Algorithm + ScheduleHint + ProofIdx + AffineToken/ReadLease.
  Because the AI Agent emits explicit schedule hints and safety witnesses alongside the algorithm, the Rul
  compiler performs zero type inference and zero search: a single-pass O(N) linear verifier mathematically
  guarantees 100% absence of memory aliasing, use-after-consume, buffer overflows, and sandbox capability
  violations in under 1 millisecond, while the 3-tier execution engine and direct x86_64 ELF64 AOT compiler
  fuse multi-stage columnar pipelines into single-pass register loops.
